+# An ASDG proposal, using the installed OpenSpec workflow
+
+This increment adds **ASDG openspec propose**: one thin wrapper that reads the project's evidence, uses the installed native workflow and links the resulting change back to its sources. It creates no real SpeakerCoach proposal yet.
+
+![ASDG evidence feeds a thin wrapper, then the installed OpenSpec workflow; one authoritative change links back to its sources and stops for review.](../../../asdg/skills/asdg-openspec-propose/images/proposal-flow.svg)
+
+The canonical [skill](../../../asdg/skills/asdg-openspec-propose/SKILL.md) and [evidence contract](../../../asdg/skills/asdg-openspec-propose/evidence.md) preserve existing command meanings. `asdg-prepare-plan`, `asdg-propose-architecture` and `openspec-propose` are unchanged. This adds a skill, not a terminal subcommand.
+
+## Discovery and scope
+
+Codex's live skill catalogue exposed all six installed OpenSpec skills: propose, explore, update-change, apply-change, sync-specs and archive-change. Their discovery was observed independently of reading `SKILL.md`; the full installed propose instructions were then read.
+OpenSpec CLI 1.15.0 resolved this client and reported no changes. Native discovery of the newly added ASDG wrapper in a fresh picker remains unverified; its adapter is installed and structurally verified.
+The current chat selected subject **OpenSpec integration**, preserving Governance and NoAttitude; native title readback matched `00 Governance OpenSpec integration`.
+Starting revision: `c7b911964f0c558849f17ab0edaec8aa89adeeec`. The native OpenSpec installation and `openspec/` were already untracked; they are preserved and excluded from this increment's diff.
+
+## What changed
+
+- Canonical wrapper, evidence/traceability contract, bounded verification cases and explanatory SVG under `asdg/skills/asdg-openspec-propose/`.
+- Thin adapter and UI metadata in both `asdg/templates/.agents/skills/asdg-openspec-propose/` and the installed `.agents/skills/asdg-openspec-propose/`.
+- Shared skill index; one relocation/preservation regression and its Markdown companions; this report/index and exact-hash AI modification receipts.
+
+The wrapper reads Purpose, Use Cases, Evaluation, Architecture and current Planning/state. It distinguishes current acceptance, stale approval, drafts and stakeholder direction, then follows the installed schema and paths. Source hashes/links live in the change; ASDG sources and OpenSpec artifacts are not mirrored.
+
+## Evidence and limits
+
+| Check | Observed result |
+| --- | --- |
+| ASDG structure | `python3 asdg/scripts/cli.py verify` passes. |
+| Regression suite | `TMPDIR=/private/tmp python3 -B -m unittest discover -s asdg/tests -p 'test_*.py'`: 59 passed on Python 3.15.0. |
+| Initial test run | Two path-comparison failures under macOS `/var` versus `/private/var`; the new test normalizes its expected path, and the documented TMPDIR fixes the existing test environment. |
+| Native CLI smoke test | A disposable fixture produced proposal, delta spec, design and tasks; 4/4 complete and strict validation passed with zero issues. |
+| Fixture traceability | Ten links resolve; five draft source hashes match; 424 pre-existing fixture files remained byte-identical. No accepted decisions were fabricated. |
+| Real project preservation | Initial 45-path snapshot unchanged before appending documentation receipts; upstream skills, application, hooks and lifecycle/sprint state remain unchanged. |
+| Package check | Eight existing external presentation-link errors in unchanged `asdg/README.md`; no new errors. |
+| Other checks | Whitespace and source-line limits pass. Generic skill validator unavailable because PyYAML is absent; no dependency installed. |
+
+The smoke test exercises the installed CLI, schema and provenance format; it is self-authored integration evidence, not an independent agent test of every instruction. Separate stores, collisions, denied writes, missing-native-skill handling and a fresh wrapper invocation remain unexercised.
+The wrapper/evidence pages and this report embed the new SVG, inspected at 720 px; the test companion's existing diagram was also inspected. These were asset rendering checks, not full Markdown preview checks. Fixture Mermaid rendering was not checked.
+
+## First real proposal
+
+Use the invocation in the [validation receipt](02.11-review-openspec-proposal-wrapper.json). It targets UC-04 as possible next-sprint work and asks for material conflicts before drafting.
+Current status marks Evaluation and Architecture accepted, but Purpose and Use Cases stale. UC-04 proposes explicit confirmation while the accepted architecture describes evidence-driven promotion; Purpose also requires distinguishing both speakers while UC-04 allows Pablo-only input. These are review decisions, not choices this wrapper makes silently.
+SPRINT-000 remains the existing streaming/agent POC. No application implementation, actual feature proposal, approval, sprint transition, commit or push occurred.
+
+[Exact increment diff](02.11-review-openspec-proposal-wrapper.diff) · [Validation receipt and changed paths](02.11-review-openspec-proposal-wrapper.json)
